# Button Component Guidelines

This guide outlines the conventions for implementing and using button components throughout the application.

## Button Types

Our codebase includes several specialized button components:

- **Basic Buttons**: Standard HTML/DaisyUI buttons
- **[ButtonGradient.js](mdc:components/ButtonGradient.js)**: Animated gradient buttons for emphasis
- **[ButtonAccount.js](mdc:components/ButtonAccount.js)**: User account dropdown button
- **[ButtonCheckout.js](mdc:components/ButtonCheckout.js)**: Stripe payment button
- **[ButtonLead.js](mdc:components/ButtonLead.js)**: Email collection form with button
- **[ButtonPopover.js](mdc:components/ButtonPopover.js)**: Button with popover menu 
- **[ButtonSignin.js](mdc:components/ButtonSignin.js)**: Authentication button
- **[ButtonSupport.js](mdc:components/ButtonSupport.js)**: Support/help button

## Basic Button Structure

- **Use DaisyUI Button Classes**
  - Base class: `btn`
  - Style variants: `btn-primary`, `btn-secondary`, `btn-accent`, etc.
  - Size variants: `btn-xs`, `btn-sm`, `btn-lg`
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Use DaisyUI button classes
  <button className="btn btn-primary">Click Me</button>
  
  // ✅ DO: Use size variants when appropriate
  <button className="btn btn-sm btn-ghost">Small Action</button>
  ```

- **Next.js Link as Button**
  - When a button navigates to another page, use Next.js Link with button styling
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Use Link for navigation buttons
  <Link href="/dashboard" className="btn btn-primary">
    Go to Dashboard
  </Link>
  ```

## Loading States

- **Show Loading Indicator**
  - Use the loading spinner during async operations
  - Disable the button while loading
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Show loading state
  <button 
    className="btn btn-primary" 
    onClick={handleAction}
    disabled={isLoading}
  >
    {isLoading ? (
      <span className="loading loading-spinner loading-xs"></span>
    ) : (
      "Submit"
    )}
  </button>
  ```

## Button with Icons

- **Icon Placement**
  - Left icon: For action identification
  - Right icon: For direction/progression indication
  - Use appropriate spacing with gap classes
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Left icon for identification
  <button className="btn btn-primary flex items-center gap-2 group">
    <svg className="w-5 h-5" fill="currentColor">
      {/* SVG paths */}
    </svg>
    <span>Save Changes</span>
  </button>
  
  // ✅ DO: Right icon for direction
  <button className="btn btn-primary flex items-center gap-2">
    <span>Next Step</span>
    <svg className="w-5 h-5" fill="currentColor">
      {/* SVG paths */}
    </svg>
  </button>
  ```

## Button Groups

- **Button Group Layout**
  - Use container with appropriate spacing
  - For connected button groups, use the `join` class from DaisyUI
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Space separate buttons
  <div className="flex gap-2">
    <button className="btn">Cancel</button>
    <button className="btn btn-primary">Save</button>
  </div>
  
  // ✅ DO: Join connected buttons
  <div className="join">
    <button className="btn join-item">Previous</button>
    <button className="btn join-item">Next</button>
  </div>
  ```

## Specialized Button Components

- **Use Specialized Buttons For Specific Use Cases**
  - Use purpose-built components for common patterns
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Use specialized button components
  <ButtonCheckout priceId="price_123" />
  
  <ButtonSignin text="Login" extraStyle="btn-secondary" />
  ```

- **Customizing Specialized Buttons**
  - Pass standardized props like `extraStyle` for styling
  - Follow the component's API pattern
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Use standard customization props
  <ButtonSignin extraStyle="btn-ghost btn-sm" />
  ```

## Responsive Buttons

- **Responsive Button Text**
  - Consider different text for mobile/desktop
  - Use responsive width/padding
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Create responsive buttons
  <button className="btn btn-primary w-full md:w-auto">
    <span className="hidden md:inline">Continue to Checkout</span>
    <span className="inline md:hidden">Continue</span>
  </button>
  ```

## Extended Block Buttons

- **Full-Width Buttons**
  - Use `btn-block` for full width
  - Great for mobile or form submissions
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Use block buttons where appropriate
  <button className="btn btn-primary btn-block">
    Create Account
  </button>
  ```

## Button Hover Effects

- **Enhanced Hover States**
  - Use Tailwind group hover for advanced effects
  - Consider animations for important actions
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Create enhanced hover effects
  <button className="btn btn-primary group">
    <span>Get Started</span>
    <svg className="w-5 h-5 group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform">
      {/* SVG paths */}
    </svg>
  </button>
  ```

## Gradient Buttons

- **Use ButtonGradient Component**
  - For high-emphasis actions
  - Pass title prop for button text
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Use gradient buttons for emphasis
  <ButtonGradient title="Start Your Free Trial" onClick={handleStart} />
  ```

## Accessibility

- **Proper Button Types**
  - Use `type="button"` for non-submitting buttons
  - Use `type="submit"` only for form submission
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Specify button types
  <button type="button" onClick={handleClick}>
    Cancel
  </button>
  
  <button type="submit">
    Save Changes
  </button>
  ```

- **Descriptive Text**
  - Use clear, action-oriented text
  - Add `aria-label` when button text isn't descriptive enough
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Use descriptive button text
  <button className="btn btn-primary">
    Create New Project
  </button>
  
  // ✅ DO: Add aria-label when needed
  <button 
    className="btn btn-circle" 
    aria-label="Close dialog"
  >
    <svg>...</svg>
  </button>
  ```

## Error Handling

- **Error State Indication**
  - Show error feedback near related buttons
  - Consider button state changes for error conditions
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Handle error states
  <div>
    <button 
      className={`btn ${hasError ? 'btn-error' : 'btn-primary'}`}
      onClick={handleSubmit}
    >
      Submit
    </button>
    {hasError && (
      <p className="text-error text-sm mt-1">{errorMessage}</p>
    )}
  </div>
  ```

These guidelines ensure consistent button implementation throughout the application, improving user experience and maintainability.
